<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Da'wa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The da'wa ('summons' or 'mission') was the missionary and propaganda organisation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ismailism">Ismaili</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fatimid-caliphate">Fatimid Caliphate</a> it was a hierarchical institution that spread Ismaili doctrine and loyalty to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/imam">imam</a>-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a> across the Islamic world, playing a central role in the dynasty's rise in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> and in its governance. Divisions within the movement later contributed to the caliphate's weakening.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dawa.jpg" alt="Da'wa" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original: Institute of Knowledge Vectorization: Kaim Amin · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:UsulALFiqh.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
